{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305129,"nonce":"fJRBijqNSZu3HT9Crk/NI5FVdTM=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhgnA","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/11","origin":"github"},"title":"Zero-length files break the global offset map","message":"`get_chunk()` walks the file-size list accumulating offsets:\n\n```python\nfor filesize in filesizes:\n    if file_offset + filesize \u003e global_offset:\n        break\n    file_offset += filesize\n    file_idx += 1\n```\n\nA zero-length file never satisfies `file_offset + 0 \u003e global_offset`, so the loop always steps past it. Verified:\n\n```\nget_chunk([10, 0, 10], 10)  -\u003e  (2, 0)      # index 1, the empty file, is unreachable\n```\n\nZero-length entries are legal in torrents. They occupy no bytes in the piece stream but must still be created on disk. Today they are skipped entirely and never appear in the output.","files":null}]}